Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 reports**.

**Merged as one issue, closed on 5 October.** It held three problems, not one
([the split](/kb/incidents/4471/split)): the parser read dates month first (fixed), the booking-v3
form hinted month first (form retired), and some dates moved by one day (still open).

<Callout kind="warn">
Closed, not done. The one-day moves are a time-zone bug the parser fix does not touch. New reports
of a booking one day off go to their own ticket, not here.
</Callout>

